{"cluster_id": "C-3379", "topic": "replication", "target": "architecture/replication", "member_ids": ["B034-125"], "canonical_claim": "During sustained writes, `CasRefLedger::confirmExactRef` was available for approximately 17% of relink attempts, with about 92,000 refusals versus 19,531 proven confirmations in the measured sender lane.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#relink-confirm-busy-lane"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3380", "topic": "replication", "target": "architecture/replication", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-186"], "canonical_claim": "Quorum inserts, `SYSTEM SYNC REPLICA`, lost-replica recovery (`cloneReplica`), and `REPLACE_RANGE`/`DROP_RANGE` log entries all reduce to sequences of fetch (relink or byte) plus drop against a CA disk, but there is no integration test exercising them, and `cloneReplica` in particular can enqueue a large fan-out of GETs that each should relink and crosses the RPL-3/RPL-4 risk classes (RPL-5).", "issue_ids": ["RPL-5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1174-L1178"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3381", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B014-001", "B014-002"], "canonical_claim": "On non-Atomic engines, a database or table literally named `detached` is structurally indistinguishable from the reserved detached subdirectory in raw path strings such as `data/db/detached/<part>/...`.; The current `PartPathParser` behavior favors parsing real detached directories into the table namespace, so an exotic non-Atomic identifier named `detached` can be misparsed and `parseTableUuid` can return `nullopt` for its bare table directory.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-12-unattended-refsnaplog-stabilization.md#L60-L73"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3382", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B019-007", "B019-008", "B019-030"], "canonical_claim": "On non-Atomic tables, `data/<db>/<table>/moving/<part>/<file>` needs an explicit `moving` anchor because the right-to-left part-directory scan otherwise anchors on the inner part and creates the spurious table id `data/<db>/<table>/moving`.; The non-Atomic parser must treat both `detached` and `moving` as reserved table-level directories and anchor on the first such component after the table prefix. Additionally, The `MOVING_DIR_NAME` unit case must map `moving/<part>/<file>` to `(live namespace, <part>, <file>)`.", "issue_ids": ["S36", "U#6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca.md#L221-L231", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca.md#L269-L299", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca-design.md#L53-L57"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3383", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B020-042", "B021-010"], "canonical_claim": "The S36/S37 placement failures were card-scale bugs: CI-scale per-part sizes exceeded the hot volume's 4 MiB `max_data_part_size_bytes`, so routing correctly sent those parts to `ca`; the fix pinned per-part bytes below the cap and scaled part counts instead.; The preferred S36/S37 fix is to keep placement-check payloads below `ROUTE_THRESHOLD_BYTES` at every scale by increasing part count rather than per-part bytes; raising `max_data_part_size_bytes` is less preferred because it weakens S37's deliberate 4 MiB routing test.", "issue_ids": ["S36", "S37"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s36-s37-placement-rca.md#L46-L52", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-17-unattended-r5-r6-round.md#L104-L111"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3384", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B031-049"], "canonical_claim": "The precise incarnation debris scope is `_log`, `_snap`, `_ckpt`, and `_files`; part manifests retain `(namespace, mount-epoch, build-sequence)` identity and loose mountpoint objects are not incarnation-qualified.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-stage-b-strategic-review-fable-round3.md#corrections"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3385", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B033-100"], "canonical_claim": "Compatibility versions are narrowed before validation, so a value such as `4294967299` can truncate to `3` and pass current-version validation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3386", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B040-110"], "canonical_claim": "PartManifest and RunFile fields named format_version currently act as compatibility_version because they are passed to checkCompatibility", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#global-versioning-model"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3387", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-011"], "canonical_claim": "The standalone watermark object and the gc/checkpoint/<n> full-GC checkpoint path shown in earlier design revisions do not exist in the current code: the build-watermark floor (min_active) was merged into the mount object as part of the ack-floor GC redesign, and gc/checkpoint/<n> has no corresponding key-builder in CasLayout.h.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#pool-layout"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3388", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-033"], "canonical_claim": "docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md's own DONE/TODO/REJECTED summary table records GCS generation-token binding as DONE 2026-07-03 (via `http_client = gcs_hmac`, a GOOG4-HMAC signer plus a wire-boundary conditional dialect that maps the response ETag to the generation, live-validated end to end), which contradicts the earlier prose in the same document describing GCS binding as deferred and fail-closed pending `Cas::Probe` validation \u2014 a live doc-internal drift the consolidation should resolve in favor of the DONE status.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#L470-L497", "docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#L647"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3389", "topic": "blob key layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-008", "B004-038", "B011-066"], "canonical_claim": "The blob body key family is blobs/<algo>/<S>/<hex>, with <algo> in ch128, xxh3, or sha256 and <S> equal to the first two hex characters. Additionally, Blob keys use `blobs/<algo>/<2-char-shard>/<hex digest>`, with `<algo>` equal to `ch128`, `xxh3`, or `sha256`; the `.meta` key is the blob key plus `.meta` and staging keys are unchanged.; Blob bodies use keys shaped as `blobs/<algo>/<hex[0:2]>/<hex>`, while `gc_shards` is a separate GC reduction fan-out routed by the high 64 bits of the digest.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#key-table", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L201-L217", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-pluggable-blob-hash-design.md#paths"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3390", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-009", "B011-084", "B012-028"], "canonical_claim": "Part manifests use keys shaped as cas/manifests/<ns>/<epoch>-<seq>/<NNNNNN>.proto and are immutable.; Manifest paths use `cas/manifests/<namespace>/<writer-epoch>-<build-sequence>/<ordinal>.proto`, and every manifest, ref-log, inspection, and repair path uses shared canonical parsing and rendering.; Manifest identifiers use canonical hex paths of the form `cas/manifests/<ns>/<epoch-hex>-<seq-hex>/<ordinal-6hex>.proto`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L256-L261", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L203-L217", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#manifest-identifier"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3391", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-291", "B001-010", "B001-038", "B011-085", "B012-027"], "canonical_claim": "Ref transactions use immutable keys shaped as cas/refs/<ns>/_log/<txn_id>, while ref snapshots use immutable keys shaped as cas/refs/<ns>/_snap/<id>.proto.; Strict CAS key parsers return std::nullopt for foreign or malformed keys rather than throwing. Additionally, `blobsPrefix()` deliberately stays `POOL/blobs/` with no algo segment so a single recursive LIST returns every algo; strict key parsers (`parseBlobKey`, `parseManifestKey`, `parseRefObjectKey`) return `std::nullopt` (never throw) for foreign/malformed keys, treating them as debris rather than corruption.; Ref objects are laid out under `cas/refs/<namespace>/` as `_cleanup/<remove-txn-id>`, `_log/<txn-id>`, and `_snap/<snapshot-id>.proto`; `_log` sorts before `_snap`.; Ref object keys are `.../cas/refs/<ns>/_log/<render>`, `.../cas/refs/<ns>/_snap/<render>.proto`, and `.../cas/refs/<ns>/_cleanup/<render>`; parsing is strict and rejects non-canonical keys.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L248-L256", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L207-L217", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#3-2-key-layout-layout-caslayout-h-blobkey-parseblobkey-in-casbuild-cpp-866-confirmed", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#L93-L112", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#object-layout"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3392", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-019", "B002-004"], "canonical_claim": "Content-addressed blobs are pool-global, while ref shards and manifests are scoped per server_root_id; dedup spans replicas at the blob level.; Content blobs use keys of the form `blobs/<aa>/<blob_hash>` and are deduplicated across tables, while part manifests are immutable root-local objects with at most one structural owner.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#L243-L247", "docs/superpowers/cas/04-gc-protocol.md#object-graph"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3393", "topic": "CAS path boundary", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-022", "B002-096", "B004-036", "B035-063"], "canonical_claim": "The @cas@ suffix on a table-directory segment marks the content-addressed boundary; detached refs use the same table namespace with a detached/ prefix. Additionally, `@cas@` is a suffix on a table-directory segment, never a standalone path segment; it marks the boundary between the mirrored ClickHouse path and the immutable CAS archive. Additionally, The `@cas@` suffix on a table-directory segment is the boundary: nodes inside it are content-addressed and immutable, while nodes outside it are verbatim. Additionally, The CAS path boundary uses an `@cas@` archive suffix on the table directory, never as a standalone segment; a node is immutable exactly when it is content-addressed, and `@cas@` marks the content-addressed/verbatim boundary.", "issue_ids": ["B181"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#L231-L241", "docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#path-mapping", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#verbatim", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#blocking-gaps", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3394", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-071", "B022-038"], "canonical_claim": "Part paths are classified using an Atomic UUID anchor or a non-Atomic part-directory fallback whose final three underscore groups are decimal.; The Atomic path parser should anchor only on a three-character lowercase-hex prefix followed by a well-formed UUID sharing that prefix, preventing `data/abc/abcxyz/...` from being misclassified.", "issue_ids": ["B40"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-umbrella-review-fixes.md#task-12-tighten-partpathparsers-atomic-uuid-anchor", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/01-frontend.md#L329-L340"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3395", "topic": "verbatim object paths", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B001-076", "B003-113", "B003-114", "B004-035", "B040-107"], "canonical_claim": "Loose verbatim files use roots/<server>/<path>, while files inside a CAS archive use \u2026@cas@/_files/<name>; GC does not scan loose mountpoint objects. Additionally, Loose verbatim mountpoint objects use keys shaped as `roots/<server_root_id>/<path>` and are probed with a directory-safe `HEAD`. Additionally, Namespace files under `roots/<srid>/<ns>/_files/<name>` and loose mountpoint objects under `roots/<srid>/<path>` bypass CAS and are removed eagerly because they are not shared. Additionally, Namespace verbatim files at <prefix>/roots/<ns>/_files/<relative-path> and mountpoint objects at <prefix>/roots/<relative-path> are raw passthrough bytes whose integrity belongs to their external file formats; Namespace-level verbatim files in the reserved `@cas@/_files/` segment are served from root-shard `_files`-keyed inline bytes and bypass the blob/manifest pipeline.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L412-L430", "docs/superpowers/cas/09-read-protocol.md#verbatim-files", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#verbatim", "docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#namespace-verbatim-files"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3396", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B002-080"], "canonical_claim": "In the current object model `ObjectKind` has only `Blob`; `Tree` and `CATR` were removed, while `PartManifest` is a protobuf body embedded in root-shard state.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#object-kinds"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3397", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B002-082"], "canonical_claim": "The normative protobuf package is `clickhouse.cas.format` in `cas_format.proto`, while the CMake target remains `clickhouse_cas_proto`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#encoding-taxonomy"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3398", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B002-095"], "canonical_claim": "The physical CAS layout includes `blobs/<shard2>/<blobId>`, `cas/refs/<ns>/<shard_number>`, `cas/manifests/<ns>/<writer_epoch>/<build_seq>/<ordinal>.proto`, `gc/state`, `gc/hb`, `gc/gen/<gen>/attempt/<attempt>/`, and `gc/server-roots/<server_root_id>/{owner,epoch,mount}`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#layout-keys"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3399", "topic": "Atomic and non-Atomic namespaces", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B002-097", "B035-064"], "canonical_claim": "Atomic tables map to `store/<u3>/<uuid>@cas@`, while non-Atomic tables map to `data/<db>/<tbl>@cas@`. Additionally, CA path mirroring distinguishes Atomic `store/<u3>/<uuid>@cas@` namespaces from non-Atomic `data/<db>/<tbl>@cas@` namespaces, and numeric-tailed loose files without an `@cas@` ancestor are opaque ordinary files rather than shards.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#path-mapping", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#blocking-gaps", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-fill"]}

